From: nerves_anbernic <none@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: skip the pre-scan power-up when the slot is empty

On the Anbernic RG40XXV the second card slot (mmc2, 4022000.mmc, the
games card) is routinely empty at boot, and an empty slot costs ~1.5
seconds of every boot:

    [    2.879808] sunxi-mmc 4022000.mmc: fatal err update clk timeout
    [    3.667822] sunxi-mmc 4022000.mmc: initialized

mmc_start_host() powers the slot up before scanning unless
MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP is set. That power-up issues two set_ios
calls, and on this controller variant (allwinner,sun50i-a100-emmc --
the config without mask_data0) each one runs the "update clock"
command into sunxi_mmc_oclk_onoff()'s 750 ms busy-wait timeout when no
card is present. The probe is asynchronous, but prepare_namespace()
waits for it via wait_for_device_probe() before mounting the root
filesystem, so the two timeouts land directly on the boot critical
path -- the observed root mount follows mmc2's probe completion by
15 ms. mmc0, whose config has mask_data0, does not time out.

The power-up buys nothing when a card-detect GPIO already reports the
slot empty: mmc_rescan() checks the same GPIO and skips the scan
without touching the card power. So set MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP
when a CD GPIO is present and reads "no card" at probe time. Slots
with a card at boot, slots without a CD GPIO, and non-removable
devices keep the pre-scan power-up. A card inserted later triggers a
rescan, which powers the slot up through mmc_rescan_try_freq() as it
always has.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1443,6 +1443,20 @@
 		goto error_free_dma;

 	/*
+	 * When a card-detect GPIO says the slot is empty, the pre-scan
+	 * power-up in mmc_start_host() buys nothing: mmc_rescan() checks
+	 * the same GPIO and skips the scan. It is not free, either. On the
+	 * eMMC controller variants, which lack mask_data0, each set_ios of
+	 * the power-up sequence runs the "update clock" command into a
+	 * 750 ms timeout against the empty slot (sunxi_mmc_oclk_onoff), so
+	 * an empty slot costs ~1.5 s in probe -- which prepare_namespace()
+	 * waits out before mounting the root filesystem. Inserting a card
+	 * later triggers a rescan, and that powers the slot up as usual.
+	 */
+	if (!(mmc->caps & MMC_CAP_NONREMOVABLE) && mmc_gpio_get_cd(mmc) == 0)
+		mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP;
+
+	/*
 	 * If we don't support delay chains in the SoC, we can't use any
 	 * of the higher speed modes. Mask them out in case the device
 	 * tree specifies the properties for them, which gets added to
